     1	# Abuse Prevention (WhipNode Cloud — Private)
     2	
     3	## Threat Model
     4	
     5	WhipNode is an anonymous upload service with public read URLs. Primary abuse vectors:
     6	
     7	1. **Storage abuse**: Using free tier as free CDN/hosting
     8	2. **Queue flooding**: Overwhelming async processing pipeline
     9	3. **Bandwidth abuse**: Hot-linking files for high-traffic distribution
    10	4. **Content abuse**: Uploading prohibited content
    11	5. **Enumeration**: Attempting to guess item IDs
    12	
    13	## Abuse Budget (enforced in code)
    14	
    15	| Limit | Value | Enforcement Point |
    16	|---|---|---|
    17	| Max free upload size | 25 MiB | items-create.ts |
    18	| Max downloads/item/hour | 200 | rate limiting middleware |
    19	| Max OCR runs/IP/day | 100 | queue consumer |
    20	| Max bandwidth/IP/hour | 500 MiB | rate limiting middleware |
    21	| Max uploads/IP/hour | 20 | items-create.ts |
    22	| Max concurrent processing/IP | 5 | items-create.ts |
    23	
    24	## Controls
    25	
    26	### IP-based rate limiting
    27	- Implemented at the Worker level using CF headers
    28	- Hashed IP stored for correlation, not raw IP
    29	
    30	### Content moderation
    31	- Zoho Catalyst moderation for images
    32	- Nudity-only blocking: faces, technical content, and all non-sexual imagery allowed
    33	- Abuse reporting endpoint for user reports
    34	
    35	### ID security
    36	- 12-character cryptographically random IDs
    37	- 32-character public tokens
    38	- Entropy sufficient to resist brute-force enumeration
    39	
    40	### Expiration
    41	- 24h default, enforced by scheduled cleanup every 15 minutes
    42	- Prevents accumulation of abandoned content
    43	
    44	## Monitoring
    45	
    46	- Track abuse_reports table for patterns
    47	- Monitor upload volume by IP hash
    48	- Monitor queue depth for flooding
    49	- Alert on moderation block rate spikes
    50	
    51	## Escalation
    52	
    53	1. Automated: rate limiting, moderation blocking
    54	2. Manual review: abuse_reports with status "open"
    55	3. IP ban: add to deny list (future implementation)
     1	# Privacy
     2	
     3	## What is stored
     4	
     5	- Uploaded files (in R2 object storage)
     6	- Item metadata: ID, timestamps, status, file count, total bytes, MIME types
     7	- Optional note text provided by the user
     8	- OCR text extracted from images/PDFs
     9	- Hashed IP address and user agent (for rate limiting and abuse prevention)
    10	- For authenticated users: email, plan, API key hashes
    11	
    12	## How long it is stored
    13	
    14	- Files and derived outputs: until expiration (default 24 hours, max depends on plan)
    15	- After expiration: file data is deleted from storage within 15 minutes
    16	- Tombstone metadata (item ID, timestamps, status): may be retained for abuse prevention
    17	
    18	## What analytics are collected
    19	
    20	- Anonymous product events (page views, uploads, format fetches)
    21	- Event properties: item ID, file count, total bytes, has_note boolean, client type, output format
    22	- Analytics are privacy-preserving by default using PostHog
    23	
    24	## What is NOT collected
    25	
    26	- File contents are never sent to analytics
    27	- OCR text is never sent to analytics
    28	- Note text is never sent to analytics
    29	- Sensitive filenames are never sent to analytics
    30	- No cross-site tracking
    31	- No advertising data
    32	
    33	## Third-party services
    34	
    35	- **Cloudflare**: Infrastructure provider (Workers, R2, D1, Queues)
    36	- **Zoho Catalyst**: OCR and content moderation processing
    37	- **PostHog**: Anonymous product analytics
    38	- **Sentry**: Error tracking (no file content included)
    39	- **Stripe**: Payment processing (for paid plans only)
    40	
    41	## Self-hosting
    42	
    43	When self-hosting WhipNode Core, you control all data storage and can choose which third-party services to enable or disable.
    40	  }
